{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 44,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the choirmaster. A Maskil of the sons of Korah. We have heard with our ears, O God; our fathers have told us the work You did in their days, in the days of old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With Your hand You drove out the nations and planted our fathers there; You crushed the peoples and cast them out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it was not by their sword that they took the land; their arm did not bring them victory. It was by Your right hand, Your arm, and the light of Your face, because You favored them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You are my King, O God, who ordains victories for Jacob.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Through You we repel our foes; through Your name we trample our enemies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I do not trust in my bow, nor does my sword save me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For You save us from our enemies; You put those who hate us to shame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In God we have boasted all day long, and Your name we will praise forever. Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But You have rejected and humbled us; You no longer go forth with our armies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You have made us retreat from the foe, and those who hate us have plundered us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You have given us up as sheep to be devoured; You have scattered us among the nations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You sell Your people for nothing; no profit do You gain from their sale.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You have made us a reproach to our neighbors, a mockery and derision to those around us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You have made us a byword among the nations, a laughingstock among the peoples.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All day long my disgrace is before me, and shame has covered my face,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "at the voice of the scorner and reviler, because of the enemy, bent on revenge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All this has come upon us, though we have not forgotten You or betrayed Your covenant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our hearts have not turned back; our steps have not strayed from Your path.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But You have crushed us in the lair of jackals; You have covered us with deepest darkness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If we had forgotten the name of our God or spread out our hands to a foreign god,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "would not God have discovered, since He knows the secrets of the heart?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet for Your sake we face death all day long; we are considered as sheep to be slaughtered.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wake up, O Lord! Why are You sleeping? Arise! Do not reject us forever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why do You hide Your face and forget our affliction and oppression?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For our soul has sunk to the dust; our bodies cling to the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.44.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rise up; be our help! Redeem us on account of Your loving devotion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
